{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22691 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "Gama-Mangostin is implicated in the biological activity of SK-VLB through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Gama-Mangostin acts as a target for Carboxylesterase 2, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound is also targeted by MOVP-3, which further links Gama-Mangostin to SK-VLB. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Gama-Mangostin indirectly influences SK-VLB through the enzymatic activity of Carboxylesterase 2 and the subsequent targeting of downstream molecules. The evidence supports a dependency on the enzymatic pathway, with SK-VLB being a downstream target of multiple intermediates. The relationship is further supported by the shared targeting of SK-VLB by different compounds, suggesting a broader biological role in the context of the dataset.",
